From: Uke Linux contributors <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: remoteproc: qcom: retain Cliffs CDSP startup ownership

Add the exact Uke CDSP descriptor and a start/stop ledger for both PAS contexts,
mappings, clocks, proxy votes and firmware metadata. Stop before clients or
resources are destroyed on every failed start; retain the core power reference
when cleanup is refused. Check all three reserved regions before SCM assignment.

The CDSP boot-FDT device is permanent: its dedicated platform driver suppresses
unbind and pins this module until reboot. This avoids relying on a void remove
callback to refuse devres cleanup. Other PAS instances keep their unload policy.
Automatic boot remains disabled. DT conversion and firmware provisioning are
separate requirements. This does not establish a physical compute transaction.

Compared with MiCode 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd and Linux 7.3.1.
Retain the original Linux, Linaro, Sony and Qualcomm GPL attribution.

